<h2>How tickets to upcoming music festivals work on a resale marketplace</h2>
<p>Seat Outlet is a resale marketplace, so festival passes are priced by the seller. A pass may be above face value when a lineup is in high demand, or below face value when the date is close and the seller wants to move it. Always compare a few listings for the same festival before you decide.</p>
<p>Festival listings can look different from regular event listings, so read each description closely to see which days and access levels the pass covers. If you are new to buying online, our <a href="/how-to-buy-tickets-online">how to buy tickets online</a> guide explains each step.</p>

<h2>Pass types to look for at upcoming music festivals</h2>
<p>A <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_festival" target="_blank" rel="noopener">music festival</a> usually offers several kinds of tickets. Names vary by event, so check what the listing includes.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Single-day pass:</strong> admission for one day, good if there is one act you do not want to miss.</li>
  <li><strong>Multi-day or weekend pass:</strong> admission for the whole run, usually the best value per day.</li>
  <li><strong>VIP or premium pass:</strong> may add extras such as better viewing areas, lounges or shorter lines, depending on the festival.</li>
  <li><strong>Camping or parking add-ons:</strong> offered at some festivals, and they may be sold separately.</li>
</ul>
<p>Not every one of the upcoming music festivals offers every option, and a listing from a reseller will describe what you get. If something is unclear, ask <a href="/ticket-customer-service">customer service</a> before you buy.</p>

<h2>Venue types: from city parks to camping grounds</h2>
<h3>Urban upcoming music festivals</h3>
<p>These take place in city parks or downtown areas, so you can go home or to a hotel each night. They are easier to reach by public transit, and many have food and shade near the stages.</p>
<h3>Camping festivals</h3>
<p>Larger festivals in rural areas often have on-site or nearby camping. Plan for weather, bring what you need and check the event rules about what you can carry in.</p>
<h3>Festivals in music cities</h3>
<p>Cities known for live music add to the trip, with local venues and late-night shows. Our <a href="/city-events">city events directory</a> lets you browse by location when you want to pair a festival with a longer visit.</p>

